WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.003
Idea. Imagine you sell cupcakes at a school fair for two dollars each, and you sell forty. You receive two times forty, which is eighty dollars. That money is your revenue.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:21.902
Pay works the same way. Remuneration is the total reward paid to employees. If you earn ten dollars an hour for six hours, your pay is sixty dollars.

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:32.024
Method. Step one, find the rate: the price per item, or the pay per hour. For revenue, always use the selling price, not a cost.

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:44.741
Step two, find every quantity. Watch the time period. Five sales every month for a year means five times twelve. If there are several shops or factories, add them together first.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:52.274
Step three, multiply the rate by the total quantity. Step four, write the currency and round as asked.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:01:10.839
Worked example. Here is a real question from Paper one in November 2024, about a robot maker in Türkiye. Each battery pack sells for ninety dollars, and it sold five every month in 2023. Calculate the total revenue for the year.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:19.142
The rate is ninety dollars per pack. In one month, revenue is ninety times five, which is four hundred and fifty dollars.

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:29.938
There are twelve months in a year. Four hundred and fifty times twelve is five thousand four hundred dollars. Or, sixty packs times ninety dollars gives the same.

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:40.873
Common mistake. The most common mistake is stopping at one month. Four hundred and fifty dollars is only one month. The question asked for the whole year.

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:50.590
Another mistake is multiplying only one group. If two shops each sell goods, add both shops' sales before you multiply by the price.

00:01:51.700 --> 00:02:04.973
Your turn. Now you try. A café employs three workers. Each works twenty-five hours a week at eight dollars fifty an hour. Calculate the café's total weekly pay. Pause here and work it out.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:14.187
Answer. First, the total quantity. Three workers each work twenty-five hours, so that is seventy-five hours a week.

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:23.004
Now multiply by the rate. Seventy-five times eight dollars fifty is six hundred and thirty-seven dollars fifty a week.

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:32.430
Remember the method: find the rate, find every quantity including the time period, then multiply. Now try the practice questions.
